VERDICT: APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS

The contact section has been correctly extracted into an independently imported component, and the live validation flow, submit gating, and final submit-time validation are functional. Production build and TypeScript validation both pass.

The only material follow-up is that the UI advertises a 500-character message maximum, but validation never enforces it and the textarea has no `maxLength`; messages over 500 characters are shown as valid and can be sent. Either enforce the stated maximum in `validateMessage`/the textarea or remove the maximum claim. There is also an unused duplicate change handler, which is harmless but should be removed during cleanup.

Security: none observed; the EmailJS identifiers were moved from the existing implementation rather than newly introduced.

Next actions: enforce or remove the advertised message maximum; optionally remove the dead handler; commit the reviewed working-tree changes before reporting completion.

